<title>INDIA: India soybean prices steady in quiet trade.</title>
<headline>India soybean prices steady in quiet trade.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were mostly steady in central Indian markets on Tuesday but prices eased by 50 rupees per tonne for some varieties, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were unchanged in thin, dull trade.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady. Soymeal yellow fetched $281-282 per tonne for export. Rapeseed extraction was quoted at $116-117 for ready shipment and at $110-111 for March-April. It was quoted at 4,000 rupees FOR Bedibunder for ready shipment and at 3,850 rupees for March-April shipment.</p>
